      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "the feature works as intended:\nyour status being BLUE, it will auto-accepts any incoming join request, regardless if your in an invite+ or friends only. \nit will travel it's chain, to the instance creator (assuming it's not you)\nthe instance creator may be green, then he will see a request that you (being blue) have accepted/forwarded for someone to join \n(if you're allowed to accept it depending on world privacy, you can't accept and won't be accepting an \"invite only\" that you are not the creator)\nif your both being in blue status, then people will get an invite to the world since all player in the chain accepted the invite prompt.\nTL:DR - Blue status auto-accepts any requests and will forward it to the \"instance owner\" who may also be blue and not see the request",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-06-14T17:55:03.304Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Last night I was in an invite+ world, with another person who had their status set to blue/auto-accept invite requests. We had two random people join on us at separate times. Neither of them were our friends.\nI guess that anyone can request an invitation from anyone, even if they are not friends, but this seems like odd behaviour - i.e. why would people be searching random names/world IDs and requesting an invite.\nPerhaps this is intended behaviour of invite+/auto-accept, but maybe it ought to only work if you have a friend in the instance.\nIf this isn't a bug, it could be moved to feature requests.",
